\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs28\b REPORT NESTED STYLES\b0\fs22\par
\par
\b PURPOSE\b0\par
USFM 3 requires a '+' prefix on any character style nested inside another marker's content -- for example, inside a footnote (\\f...\\f*), a cross-reference style must be written \\+xt...\\+xt*, not bare \\xt...\\xt*. This check scans selected books for footnotes and flags any character style used inside one that is missing its required '+'.\par
\par
Only markers your project's usfm.sty/custom.sty actually declare as a character style are checked. Footnote-internal markers (\\fr, \\fq, \\fqa, \\fk, \\fl, \\fp, \\ft, \\fv, \\fdc, \\fm) are never flagged -- they're the footnote's own structure, not a nested style. Each opening and closing marker token is checked independently, so a mismatched pair (for example \\+it opened correctly but closed as plain \\it*) is caught on the specific token that's wrong.\par
\par
Results appear in two places:\par
- The results list shows one row per flagged footnote, with the marker(s) found missing their '+' (e.g. "Missing +: xt"). Clicking a row jumps to that footnote in the text. Footnotes with no issues do not appear here.\par
- A NestedStylesReport.html report is written: a summary of how many footnotes were scanned and flagged, plus a breakdown of how many times each marker was found missing its '+', followed by every flagged footnote shown with its markers displayed -- the specific marker(s) missing '+' highlighted in red. Footnotes with no issues are not shown in the report. The report opens automatically in your browser after the check runs.\par
\par
If anything unexpected happens, a NestedStylesDebug.log file will appear in the project folder with the details - please share its contents so the check can be fixed.\par
\par
\b HOW TO USE\b0\par
1. Install the Phils Custom (cms) Checks plugin with Install_Phils_tools.exe. Everything comes with the plugin: nothing has to be copied into the cms folder. References in the HTML report can be clicked to show that place in Paratext. The first click makes the browser ask whether to open ParatextGoTo, and Paratext follows only when the text window's scroll group follows other programs.\par
2. In Paratext, choose Tools > Phils Custom (cms) Checks..., select this check and click "Run...". In Paratext's check window, choose the books and set the options (Options...) before you click OK.\par
3. Review the results list to jump to each flagged footnote, and the NestedStylesReport.html report (opened automatically) to see every flagged footnote with the offending marker(s) highlighted in red.\par
}
